      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In Brussels, the decision-making epicenter of the European Union, regulators have rejected a proposed new path forward from the search engine operator. This move follows more than two years of proceedings under the bloc's gatekeeper rules, as authorities finalize a penalty expected to reach the high hundreds of millions of euros. The formal decision is anticipated before the Commission's August recess, adding to a long trail of accumulated fines for Alphabet.",
